<title>SINGAPORE: India tenders to sell 50,000/T of Sept naphtha.</title>
<headline>India tenders to sell 50,000/T of Sept naphtha.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has offered to sell through two tenders 50,000 tonnes of naphtha lifting in September, traders said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Traders said IOC is offering 25,000 tonnes of low aromatic naphtha lifting from Bombay on the west coast between September 22-24 and 25,000 tonnes of natural gas liquids (NGL) lifting from Hazira between September 14-16.</p>
<p>Both tenders close on September 5.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
